EX-J28 ANS+LZ77 candidate for block_ctx_map encoding (2026-05-28)
==================================================================

Change: jxl-encoder/src/vardct/context_tree.rs:write_context_map_from_slice
now compares 4 candidates (Simple, Huffman, Huffman+MTF, ANS+LZ77) and
picks the cheapest by trial-encoded bit count. Previously only the first
three were compared. libjxl `EncodeContextMap` uses BuildAndEncodeHistograms
which includes ANS+LZ77 with HybridUintConfig(2,0,1), so this restores parity.

Env hook: JXL_NO_ANS_LZ77_CTXMAP=1 disables the new candidate.

50-file paired A/B:
  Sample seeded by random.seed(11), mixed corpus.
  cjxl-e7:       10,069,483 B
  ours-e7 OFF:   10,178,807 B  Δ +1.086% vs cjxl
  ours-e7 ON:    10,178,736 B  Δ +1.085% vs cjxl
  ON vs OFF:     -0.001%  (-71 B)
  Roundtrip:     50/50 byte-identical via djxl --reconstruct_jpeg

Acceptance gates:
- (a) Build PASS
- (b) Hash-locks 36/36 BYTE-IDENTICAL (synthetic fixtures don't change
       block_ctx_map encoding pick — kBest/Simple choices unchanged)
- (c) ON < OFF on 50-file paired bench (-71 B, strict)
- (d) 50/50 roundtrip OK via djxl

Notes:
- Tiny per-file gain (~1.4 B/file) but it's strictly better and removes
  a real libjxl divergence in the selector.
- The new candidate may shift more bytes on larger/more-complex block
  context maps (e.g. multi-strategy VarDct paths beyond JPEG transcode);
  those paths unaffected because synthetic-tested cases keep their existing
  Simple/Huffman picks.

DO NOT (future agents):
- DO NOT remove the env hook; it's needed for A/B against future
  optimizations of the ANS+LZ77 path itself.
- DO NOT cite "FMA precision" for the -71 byte delta — this is a
  histogram-cost-comparison + encoder format choice, not a numeric
  artifact.
